              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Despite his name, **Flounder is not actually a flounder**. Real flounders are flat, camouflaged, brown fish that live on the ocean floor and have both of their eyes on one side of their head. \n\nHis actual species depends on whether you are looking at the original animated movie or the live-action remake:\n\n### 1. In the 1989 Animated Film: A Stylized Tropical Fish (often associated with Angelfish)\nIn the original cartoon, Flounder is a stylized, round, brightly colored tropical reef fish. \n* **Design inspiration:** The animators didn't design him to be one specific species, but his bright yellow body and blue/teal stripes closely resemble a **blue angelfish** or a **yellowtail damselfish**. \n* **The \"Guppy\" nickname:** Throughout the movie and the animated series, Ariel and other characters tease him by calling him a **\"guppy\"** because of his cowardly and anxious personality, but this is a nickname rather than his actual species.\n\n### 2. In the 2023 Live-Action Remake: A Sergeant Major Fish\nFor the 2023 live-action adaptation, Disney opted for a photorealistic look and officially modeled Flounder's design after a **sergeant major fish** (*Abudefduf saxatilis*). \n* This is a species of damselfish native to the Atlantic Ocean that features a round, flat-sided body with yellow and silver coloring and vertical dark blue/black stripes.",
